# This repository IS the webroot. Anything committed here is a file nginx will
# be asked to serve, so the ignore list is a security control, not tidiness.
# It is the second layer; the vhost 404s these classes too. Neither layer is
# allowed to be the only one.

# -- Editor and backup droppings ---------------------------------------------
# The exact class of file that caused the 2026-08-08 webroot exposure on the
# ita vhost.
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.rej
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# -- Ops, status and working notes -------------------------------------------
# Session status reports, run logs, deploy notes, handover docs and authoring
# notes. These describe the infrastructure, name paths, and sometimes quote
# config — none of it belongs in a public repository, and none of it belongs in
# a directory a web server is pointed at. The webroot is both.
#
# The pattern is deliberately broad: a note-class file is far more likely to be
# created under a name nobody predicted than to be created under one of these.
STATUS-*
STATUS-*.md
*-STATUS.md
*-status.md
CONTENT-NOTES.md
*-NOTES.md
*-notes.md
NOTES.md
TODO.md
HANDOVER*.md
RUNBOOK*.md
DEPLOY-NOTES*.md
*.draft
*.draft.*
drafts/
notes/
.cc-status/

# -- Logs ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/

# -- Anything credential-shaped ----------------------------------------------
# Nothing here should ever hold a secret — the site has no backend and makes no
# authenticated calls. This block exists so that stays true by accident as well
# as by design.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.credentials
credentials*
secrets*
.netrc

# -- Working files that must never reach a webroot ---------------------------
*.tmp
*.temp
scratch/
staging/
tmp/

# -- Build inputs, if a build step is ever added ------------------------------
node_modules/
package-lock.json
